Conclusion
Ceramic coating myths often create expectations that were never realistic, from claims of complete scratch protection to the idea that coated cars never need maintenance. Understanding the actual capabilities and limitations of ceramic coating helps you make a more informed decision.
Proper paint preparation, professional application, suitable maintenance, and realistic expectations all play an important role in getting the most from ceramic paint protection.
Frequently Asked Questions
Is ceramic coating really scratch-proof? No, ceramic coating is not scratch-proof. It helps reduce light swirl marks and minor scuffs, but deeper scratches from sharp objects can still happen.
Do coated cars still need regular washing? Yes, coated cars still need regular washing to stay clean and perform well. The coating just makes dirt and grime easier to rinse off during each wash.
How long does ceramic coating actually last? Ceramic coating typically lasts 1 to 2 years for consumer-grade products and 3 to 5 years or more for professional-grade coatings. Regular maintenance helps it last closer to the higher end.
Can ceramic coating cause problems if applied incorrectly? Yes, poor application or inadequate paint prep can lead to issues like uneven curing or trapped contaminants. Choosing an experienced installer helps avoid most common problems.
